[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue with one fix queued. Read report by report, it
holds three problems, and one fix closes only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix closed #4471, but not its other two problems. The booking-v3 form hint and the
one-day shift need their own fixes, so each has its own ticket.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## The three problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first, so a date with a day of 12 or less flips: "Our 7 April reminder went out on 4 July." It
comes in by app, email and form, from every tenant. This is the bug #4471 named.

**`hint` — the booking-v3 form tells people to type month first.** Its date field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY`, people type what it says, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first.
The date flips the same way, but the parser is not involved: it only comes in by `form`, and only
from tenants that run booking-v3. Changing the parser leaves it as it is; the hint has to change.

**`shift` — the date moves by one day.** "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got
Monday. Same meeting." Swapping day and month cannot move a date by one day, so these are not the
parser, even though their tenants write the day first. The pattern — a weekday off, a different
day per time zone, "only June", an invite that arrived before the booking — points at time-zone
or daylight-saving handling. The desk had already read them as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`) and still files them by tenant, so the table counts them under `parser`
too, the way the desk's own view does; they still need their own fix.

## How they were told apart

- Counted by id, not by row: the ticket export pages overlap.
- Not by intake's tag: it is a guess from the reporter's browser, and it is wrong for many of them.
- Not by subject: [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone,
  and every problem here shares the same dozen subjects. That is how three problems became one
  ticket.
- By what the report says and where it comes from: the tenant's locale and booking form
  (`causes.ts`), the channel, and the body.

## Next

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October:

- `parser` — fixed ("fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales"). [#1](https://github.com/zinit/support-kb-4471/issues/1) is closed.
- `hint` — won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired, so no new reports of this kind can come in.
  [#2](https://github.com/zinit/support-kb-4471/issues/2) is closed as not planned.
- `shift` — not in the update, and neither fix touches time-zone or daylight-saving handling. It
  is the one problem from #4471 still open: [#3](https://github.com/zinit/support-kb-4471/issues/3)
  stays open until engineering takes it.
- Decision 0001 and the triage page have not been reviewed since 2024. Subject matching can't
  separate these problems, so it needs a new decision record.

